      "statement": "HeaderSectorReader backs the ISO walk with the IRD's embedded header buffer, always returning a full 2048-byte sector and zero-filling past the header end; without that the vendored read_bytes would spin forever on a short sector (a guard was added upstream-side too) or abort the whole walk, since IRDs carry only the volume descriptors and directory extents.",
